  <p class="guide-body-note"><strong>Use one unit system.</strong> Circle inches or centimeters. A uses supported posture; E uses lying posture with a natural bend. Leave A pending if supported standing is not comfortable. Do not substitute E for A.</p>
  <div class="guide-meta"><div>Supported posture / helper: _______________________</div><div>Widest location / asymmetry: _____________________</div></div>
  <p class="guide-body-note"><strong>Before sharing:</strong> repeat the measurement; confirm the same landmarks and units. Note thick coat, posture changes or differences between sides. Buddy’s 140 lb is owner reported; all of his body dimensions are still pending until measured.</p>
  <p class="guide-body-note">Body measurements are not CAD settings. Harness offsets, padding, tire deflection, clearances and suspension movement need separate engineering and fitting review. A completed worksheet does not approve a fit or establish a load capacity.</p>
  <p class="guide-body-note">Method references: <a href="https://walkinpets.com/pages/wheelchair-sizer/">Walkin’ Pets rear-leg guide</a>; <a href="https://eddieswheels.com/files/A_Visual_Guide_to_Measuring_Your_Pet_-_Eddies_Wheels_for_Pets_-_The_Pet_Mobility_Experts.pdf">Eddie’s Wheels supported-measurement guide</a>. <a href="https://ruffwear.com/blogs/explored/the-size-is-right-how-to-measure-for-your-dogs-gear">Ruffwear’s girth guide</a> explains the chest landmark; follow the selected harness supplier’s instructions separately. Methods and codes differ between brands.</p>
